dule path github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ts/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Full ts implementation -- flag parsing, stdin reading loop, default/custom/subsecond/incremental/elapsed/monotonic modes. Excludes -r mode (prd004-ts R6), which is deferred to a follow-up task.\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement default timestamp mode (prd004-ts R1.1-R1.6): read stdin line by line using bufio.Scanner, prepend a strftime-formatted wall-clock timestamp and a single space to each line, flush stdout after each line via bufio.Writer, pass through partial lines at EOF (no trailing newline added), exit 0 on clean EOF. The default format string is '%b %d %H:%M:%S'.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement custom strftime format string support (prd004-ts R2.1-R2.4): accept an optional positional argument containing a strftime format string. Convert strftime percent-specifiers to Go time.Format reference-time tokens (%Y->2006, %m->01, %d->02, %H->15, %M->04, %S->05, %b->Jan, %B->January, %A->Monday, %a->Mon, %Z->MST, %z->-0700, %j->002, %p->PM, %e->_2, unknown specifiers passed through unchanged). Support the ts-specific subsecond extensions %.S (seconds.microseconds e.g. '32.001234'), %.s (unix-epoch.microseconds e.g. '1708358732.001234'), %.T (HH:MM:SS.microseconds e.g. '14:05:32.001234') by detecting and substituting them before the strftime conversion pass, using a single time.Now() call per line for both second and microsecond components.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement -i incremental mode (prd004-ts R3.1-R3.4): timestamp shows elapsed time since the previous line was received (first line shows elapsed since ts started). Default format '%H:%M:%S'. Format elapsed duration using time.Unix(int64(d.Seconds()), 0).UTC().Format(goFmt) to match strftime(fmt, gmtime(delta)) Perl source behavior. -i and -s are mutually exclusive -- if both are given, print a usage message to stderr and exit non-zero.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement -s elapsed-since-start mode (prd004-ts R4.1-R4.3): timestamp shows monotonically increasing elapsed time since ts started, using the same duration-as-UTC-wall-clock formatting as -i. Default format '%H:%M:%S'. A custom format argument overrides the default.\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Implement -m monotonic clock mode (prd004-ts R5.1-R5.3): use the monotonic reading embedded in time.Now() for all timestamp sampling. Compatible with default mode, -i, -s, and all custom format strings including subsecond extensions. When -m is active, the timestamp source must not jump on wall-clock adjustments.\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Implement exit codes and SIGPIPE handling (prd004-ts R7.1-R7.2): exit 0 on clean EOF; exit non-zero and print a usage message to stderr when an unrecognized flag is given. Call signal.Ignore(syscall.SIGPIPE) at program startup. After each write to stdout, if the error is a broken-pipe error (syscall.EPIPE or io.ErrClosedPipe), exit 0 silently without printing an error message. Do not import pkg/sys -- ts has no pkg/sys dependency per the dependency map.\"\n      - id: R7\n        text: \"Implement TZ environment handling (prd004-ts R8.1-R8.2): for wall-clock timestamp modes (default and custom format without -i/-s), resolve the local timezone from the TZ environment variable using time.LoadLocation(os.Getenv('TZ')); if TZ is unset or invalid, fall back to time.Local. For -i and -s elapsed modes, always use time.UTC for formatting regardless of the TZ environment variable.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"strftime-to-Go conversion: implement a convertFormat(strftimeFmt string) (goFmt string, hasSubsecond bool, subsecondKind string) function that first scans the format string for the three subsecond extensions (%.S, %.s, %.T), replaces them with unique sentinel tokens, then walks character by character replacing known strftime specifiers with Go reference-time tokens, and returns the converted format plus metadata about subsecond handling.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Subsecond extension substitution: after formatting the wall-clock or elapsed time via time.Format, do a second pass replacing the sentinel tokens for %.S/%.s/%.T with the computed microsecond strings derived from the same time.Now() sample captured at the start of each line's processing.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Elapsed-time formatting for -i and -s: compute duration d as time.Duration, then format using time.Unix(int64(d.Seconds()), 0).UTC().Format(goFmt). This matches the Perl source behavior of calling strftime(fmt, gmtime(int(delta))) with TZ=GMT, so that a 5-second delta produces '00:00:05' with the default '%H:%M:%S' format.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"The binary is package main under cmd/ts/. The go.mod module is github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils. Use os/signal, syscall, bufio, fmt, os, strings, time -- all stdlib. No external or internal package imports are needed for this implementation. Flag parsing uses the standard flag package; the positional format argument is retrieved via flag.Args() after flag.Parse().\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"'go build ./cmd/ts/' succeeds and produces a binary. 'golangci-lint run ./cmd/ts/' reports zero warnings or errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"printf 'line1\\\\nline2\\\\nline3\\\\n' | ./bin/ts produces exactly three output lines, each starting with a timestamp matching the pattern of '%b %d %H:%M:%S' (e.g. 'Feb 27 15:04:05 line1') followed by a single space and the original line content.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"printf 'a\\\\nb\\\\nc\\\\n' | ./bin/ts -s produces three lines with HH:MM:SS elapsed timestamps that are monotonically non-decreasing (each timestamp >= the previous one).\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"printf 'first\\\\nsecond\\\\nthird\\\\n' | ./bin/ts -i produces three lines, each with an HH:MM:SS incremental timestamp showing time since the previous line.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"./bin/ts -i -s exits non-zero and writes a usage message to stderr. stdout must be empty.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"./bin/ts -z exits non-zero and writes a usage message to stderr (unrecognized flag).\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"printf '' | ./bin/ts (empty stdin, immediate EOF) produces no output on stdout, no output on stderr, and exits 0.\"\n      - id: AC8\n        text: \"printf 'partial' | ./bin/ts (stdin with no trailing newline) produces exactly one output line prefixed with a timestamp and space, with no extra newline appended beyond what was in the input.\"\n      - id: AC9\n        text: \"printf 'tick\\\\n' | ./bin/ts '%.S' produces one line with a 'seconds.microseconds' prefix (e.g. '1740672000.001234 tick') where the microseconds field has exactly 6 decimal digits.\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"9f42cd5a-1743-418a-a045-f5a4dc0bd662","total_cost_usd":0.7498895,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":73796,"cache_read_input_tokens":15559,"output_tokens":11235,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":73796,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":11235,"cacheReadInputTokens":15559,"cacheCreationInputTokens":73796,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7498895,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"eedb6a9d-6c52-48a6-9976-21635611c2f2"}
